[Term]
id: GO:0003823
name: antigen binding
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Binding to an antigen, any substance which is capable of inducing a specific immune response and of reacting with the products of that response, the specific antibody or specifically sensitized T-lymphocytes, or both. Binding may counteract the biological activity of the antigen. Antigen binding by an MHC protein complex allows the antigen to be displayed to a T cell or NK cell." [GOC:jl, ISBN:0198506732, ISBN:0721662544]
