[Term]
id: GO:0035175
name: histone H3S10 kinase activity
namespace: molecular_function
alt_id: GO:0044021
def: "Catalysis of the reaction: histone H3-serine (position 10) + ATP = histone H3-phosphoserine (position 10) + ADP. This reaction is the addition of a phosphate group to the serine residue at position 10 of histone H3." [GOC:bf, PMID:15041176]
comment: Comment: Note that the residue position corresponds to the canonical human H3 histone (UniProtKB:P84243); this residue is conserved across all eukaryotes. Residue 1 is the first residue following removal of the initiating Methionine (Met). Note that each histone is encoded by multiple genes, and sequences may vary across different genes within an organism.
synonym: "histone kinase activity (H3-S10 specific)" EXACT []
synonym: "histone serine kinase activity (H3-S10 specific)" EXACT []
