def: "Catalysis of the reaction: histone H2AX-serine (position 139) + ATP = histone H2AX-phosphoserine (position 139) + ADP. This reaction is the addition of a phosphate group to the serine residue at position 139 of histone variant H2AX." [PMID:11893489, PMID:16061642]
comment: Note that the residue position corresponds to the canonical human H2AX histone (UniProtKB:P16104); this residue is conserved across all eukaryotes. Residue 1 is the first residue following removal of the initiating Methionine (Met). Note that each histone is encoded by multiple genes, and sequences may vary across different genes within an organism.
synonym: "histone H2AS139 kinase activity" RELATED []
synonym: "histone kinase activity (H2A-S139 specific)" RELATED []
synonym: "histone kinase activity (H2A.x-S139 specific)" NARROW [GOC:bf, PMID:16061642]
