comment: Note that the residue position corresponds to the canonical human H2A2A histone (UniProtKB:Q6FI13); this residue is conserved across all eukaryotes, but missing from Drosophila histone H2AV. Residue 1 is the first residue following removal of the initiating Methionine (Met). Note that each histone is encoded by multiple genes, and sequences may vary across different genes within an organism.
