[Term]
id: GO:0044025
name: histone H2BS14 kinase activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Catalysis of the reaction: histone H2B-serine (position 14) + ATP = histone H2B-phosphoserine (position 14) + ADP. This reaction is the addition of a phosphate group to the serine residue at position 14 of histone H2B." [PMID:15652479]
comment: Note that the residue position corresponds to the canonical human H2B histone (UniProtKB:P62807); the N-terminus of histone H2B is divergent across eukaryotes; make sure that the paper clearly references the human protein for the position of this modification to use this term. Residue 1 is the first residue following removal of the initiating Methionine (Met). Corresponds to Serine 10 in yeast (PMID:15652479). Note that each histone is encoded by multiple genes, and sequences may vary across different genes within an organism.
synonym: "histone kinase activity (H2B-S14 specific)" EXACT []
synonym: "histone serine kinase activity (H2B-S14 specific)" EXACT []
